  "finding": "Doubling the per-buffer limit widened main transforms from 16 to 32 columns, increased transform device time by about one second per trial and slowed complete trial time by about 2%. Keeping 1 GiB buffers with a 9 GiB managed budget reduced median trial time by 0.31%, or 0.39% with scratch reuse. The sample does not establish a substantial or general speedup.",
  "decision": "Retain the existing 7 GiB managed budget, 1 GiB buffer limit, and disabled transform scratch cache. Experimental variants remain available through the benchmark runner.",
